---
source: crates/forgejo-core/src/error/render.rs
expression: "snap(ErrorKind::Connect\n{\n    host: \"git.example.org\".into(), port: 443, cause:\n    \"tcp connect error: Connection refused (os error 111)\".into(),\n    looks_like_plaintext: false, scheme: \"https\".into(),\n}, RequestCtx\n{\n    host: Some(\"git.example.org\".into()), method: Some(\"GET\".into()), path:\n    Some(\"/api/v1/user\".into()), ..RequestCtx::default()\n})"
---
error: cannot connect to git.example.org

  request: GET /api/v1/user
  host:    git.example.org
  port:    443
  cause:   tcp connect error: Connection refused (os error 111)

what to do:
  the hostname resolved, but the connection failed.
  1. test the same address with curl:
     curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://git.example.org:443/api/v1/version
  2. if the port is wrong, log in with the correct port (example: 3000):
     fcli auth login --host https://git.example.org:3000
  note: check whether a firewall or VPN is blocking the connection.
